    "parts": [],
    "answer_text": "DNA fingerprinting is a technique used to identify and analyze the variations in various individuals at the level of DNA. It is based on variability and polymorphism in DNA sequences. Applications include: (1) forensic science to identify potential crime suspects, (2) establishing paternity and family relationships, (3) identifying and protecting commercial varieties of crops and livestock, and (4) finding out the evolutionary history of an organism.",
    "answer_latex": null,
